  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Intransitive pair: {織|お}れる (can be woven - potential). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{織|お}る (to weave X).\n\nASPECT: て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates ongoing action. {織|お}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ = 'is weaving.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{布|ぬの}→布：01489_nuno⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{織|お}る (to weave cloth)\n- ⟦{糸|いと}→糸：01315_ito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{織|お}る (to weave thread)\n- ⟦{機|はた}→機：noentry⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{織|お}る (to weave on a loom)\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧{織|お}り (hand-woven)\n- ⟦{機|はた}→機：noentry⟧{織|お}り (weaving, loom work)\n- ⟦{織物|おりもの}→織物：10583_orimono⟧ (woven fabric, textile)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE: Weaving has a long tradition in Japan, particularly for kimono fabrics like ⟦{西陣織|にしじんおり}→西陣織：noentry⟧ (Nishijin weaving).",
